    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "\ud83d\udcbb Process Resource Diagnostics \u2014 CPU, Physical RAM (RSS), Virtual Memory & Open File Descriptors",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 50
      },
      "transparent": true,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### \ud83d\udcbb **Novice Guide: Process Resource & Memory Performance Diagnostics**\n* **Physical RAM (RSS):** Actual physical RAM occupied in hardware by the Python process (`process_resident_memory_bytes`). Normal: **300 MB \u2013 800 MB** (includes loaded FastEmbed vector models).\n* **Virtual Memory (VSZ):** Virtual memory address space allocated (`process_virtual_memory_bytes`). Includes shared libraries & thread memory maps.\n* **CPU Usage (%):** Percentage of total CPU compute consumed across Ryzen 5 3550H cores (`rate(process_cpu_seconds_total[1m]) * 100`). Normal: **< 10%** idle, **15% \u2013 30%** during burst analysis.\n* **Open File Descriptors (FDs):** Active open file handles and network sockets (`process_open_fds`). Max limit is 1024. Leak warning if FDs exceed **500**.\n* **Garbage Collection (GC):** Frequency of CPython object cleanup cycles (`python_gc_collections_total`). High rates ($>5/s$) indicate memory churn."
      }
    },
